ts Lourdes University Transfer Siena Heights Transfer International Students Graduate Programs Other Programs Admitted Students Financial Aid Visit Defiance College Admissions Staff Academics Programs Of Study Graduate Offerings Academic Support Services McMaster School for Advancing Humanity Jacket Journey: Career Readiness Carolyn M Small Honors Program Registrar DEFIne Your Summer Student Life Residence Life Ask Buzz Dining Options Health & Safety Parking Information Student Activities & Organizations Parents & Families Counseling & Accessibility Services Veterans Programs Student Life Staff Alumni Stay Connected with DC Alumni Organizations Alumni Awards DC Publications Homecoming Athletics About Leadership Board of Trustees History Campus Map & Directions Conferences & Events Higher Education Act Disclosures Admissions First Year Transfer Students Lourdes University Transfer Siena Heights Transfer International Students Graduate Programs Other Programs Admitted Students Financial Aid Visit Defiance College Admissions Staff Academics Programs Of Study Graduate Offerings Academic Support Services McMaster School for Advancing Humanity Jacket Journey: Career Readiness Carolyn M Small Honors Program Registrar DEFIne Your Summer Student Life Residence Life Ask Buzz Dining Options Health & Safety Parking Information Student Activities & Organizations Parents & Families Counseling & Accessibility Services Veterans Programs Student Life Staff Alumni Stay Connected with DC Alumni Organizations Alumni Awards DC Publications Homecoming Athletics About Leadership Board of Trustees History Campus Map & Directions Conferences & Events Higher Education Act Disclosures A comprehensive, four-year program woven into every Defiance College student’s curriculum—designed to prepare students not just for a successful career, but for a fulfilling life. Get Info Much More Than A Career Readiness Program... Jacket Journey is a career-readiness program that will help students see connections between their experience in the classroom, participation in co-curricular and extracurricular activities, and the power skills needed for success in the 21st century workplace. This program is designed to help students better articulate the knowledge, skills, and dispositions they acquire at Defiance College; foster dialogue between the college community and employers through an annual summit; and provide faculty with opportunities to connect with employers. Your education is a journey. As a Defiance College Yellow Jacket, your journey will prepare you for a lifetime of professional possibilities. While most colleges tell seniors how to react when opportunity knocks, we teach students how to open doors for themselves. The Results Speak for Themselves Through Jacket Journey, 97.5% of Defiance College graduates over the past five years have successfully launched into careers, graduate school, or military service Jacket Days Jacket Days is a multi-day, conference-style experience held on the Defiance College campus that prepares students for career success. As a key part of our commitment to workforce development and career readiness, Jacket Days connects students with industry professionals, practical learning sessions, and hands-on skill building. What Students Can Expect: Career & Discussion Panels with professionals from fields including criminal justice, education, social work, environmental science, business, and more Interactive Learning Sessions focused on career pathways, personal development, and real-world skills Skill-Building Workshops , including mock interviews and practical career preparation activities Jacket Days equips students with the skills, insights, and connections they need to confidently take the next step in their professional journey. Play Play Play Play Play Jacket Days 2026 Digital Program Jacket Summit Employer insight drives Jacket Journey, ensuring our programs stay relevant, responsive, and focused on preparing graduates to contribute from day one Learn More & RSVP How Jacket Journey Works: By the completion of this program, students will: Assemble a job-readiness portfolio that includes an applicant introduction, qualifications summary, professional resume, general cover letter, and self-reflective essay on why a particular field or career path is right for you. Summarize educational background, professional experiences, skills, qualifications and interest in a job and/or post-baccalaureate program both formally and informally. Whats the value? Develop the ability to apply career-readiness skills in pursuing your next challenge Become uniquely valuable and competitive in today’s workforce Earn points by attending Jacket Journey events and simultaneously refine the soft skills employers want to hire. Top point earners win prizes! Jacket Journey Competencies: Financial Literacy Understand and effectively use various financial skills, including personal financial management, budgeting, and investing. Oral and Written Communication Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of an organization. Critical and Creative Thinking Identify and respond to needs based upon an understanding of situational context and logical analysis of relevant information. Teamwork and Collaboration Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, while appreciating diverse viewpoints and share responsibilities. Ethical Judgment and Decision Making The ability to assess situations and make decisions based on moral principles and values, especially in challenging circumstances. Digital Technology Understand and leverage technologies ethically to enhance efficiencies, complete tasks, and accomplish goals. * These competencies are based off the career competencies defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). Resources: Individual Jacket Points Leaderboard FYE Jacket Points Leaderboard Athletics Jacket Points Leaderboard Jacket Days College Central Network Optimal Resume Our Values: To Know To Understand To Lead To Serve Defiance College graduates students to lead distinctive lives in their chosen professions through a spirit of service by preparing them To Know, To Understand, To Lead, and To Serve. Apply Today Schedule A Visit Defiance College graduates students to lead distinctive lives in their chosen professions through a spirit of service by preparing them To Know, To Understand, To Lead, and To Serve Apply Visit Get Info Facebook X-twitter Youtube Instagram Quick Links Accreditation Campus Map Employment Privacy Policy Title IX Accessibility Statement Trademark and Brand Use Statement Get In Touch Contact 800 520-4632 701 N Clinton St, Defiance, OH 43512 Site Map © Defiance College - 2025 All Rights Reserved."
